            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for a new account book, then the Bengali for a custom."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: শঙ্খ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "শঙ্খ — shôngkhô — \"a conch shell\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "সন্ধ্যায় মন্দিরে কেউ শঙ্খ বাজাল। sôndhyāy mondire keu shôngkhô bājālô. In the evening someone blew a conch at the temple."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "শঙ্খ (shôngkhô) is Sanskrit śaṅkha, a shell, above all the conch (Monier-Williams). Its ঙ্খ is ngkh; everyday speech wears the word down to শাঁখ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
